,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":718.358667069,"data":"## 3. Scientific Methodology \u0026 Research Implications\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":718.358670635,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":718.358673926,"data":"1. **Causal Perturbation Verification:**\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":718.358677945,"data":"   - Sensitivity $S = \\frac{1}{{N}} \\sum |p(x_{raw}) - p(x_{jpeg95})|$ evaluates BOTH models on the exact same two views.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":718.358681936,"data":"   - For Model A, a high $S$ proves that the network exploits the uncompressed state of synthetic PNGs.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":718.35868563,"data":"   - For Model B1, a low $S$ confirms genuine compression invariance.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":718.358689161,"data":"2. **Double Compression vs Single Compression Nuance:**\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":718.358693041,"data":"   - Real images undergo double compression; synthetic images undergo single compression.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":718.358696629,"data":"   - This diagnostic verifies whether equalizing the compression stage mitigates format asymmetry without obliterating high-frequency generative traces.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":718.358700491,"data":"3. **Next Steps for Milestone R2:**\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":718.35870385,"data":"   - Preprocessing is now mathematically adjudicated and officially sealed as **`SEAL_B1`**.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":718.358707424,"data":"   - Checkpoints for all 6 models have been saved to `checkpoints/`.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":718.358711154,"data":"   - With preprocessing locked, we proceed to official multi-seed training of **Semantic-only**, **Forensic-only**, and **Fusion** models on Kaggle GPU, and finally evaluate against held-out `in_domain_test` and all 6 `cross_generator_ood` families.\n"}
